{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210734,"nonce":"9Ogvls0vvi+vx3FP6zTE9EtTHN4=","title":"Threaded interp emitted string concat only for arity 2; 3+ chains produced null","message":"Fixed; see git log for the landing commit. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n\n```wren\nvar f = Fn.new {|x, y|\n  System.print(\"a %(x) b %(y)\")\n}\nf.call(1, 2)\n```\n\n- `--mode tiered` (default): printed `null`\n- `--mode jit`: printed `null`\n- `--mode interpreter` (MIR walker): printed `a 1 b 2`\n\n\n`Fn.new` closures take the threaded-interp baseline path. `src/mir/threaded.rs::build_threaded` only emitted an `op_string_concat` when `parts.len() == 2`. Anything wider — every 3+ slot interpolation — fell through to the catch-all `op_noop` arm, leaving the destination register uninitialised (= `Value::null()`). The `can_use_threaded` gate accepted every arity, so the function happily JIT-baselined into a path that silently dropped its concat.\n\nWider context: the MIR builder lowers `Expr::Interpolation(parts)` to `Instruction::StringConcat(vals)` where `vals` has one entry per stringified part. `\"a %(x) b %(y)\"` is 5 parts post-ToString.\n\n\nExpand multi-arity StringConcat to a chain of 2-arg `op_string_concat`s, each writing back to the same destination register. First pass's block-offset counter also accounts for the extra ops so branch fixups land correctly.\n\nRegression test: `tests/e2e.rs::e2e_threaded_multi_interp_in_closure`.\n\n\n@hatch:fsm example `examples/fsm-game-flow/main.wren` signal handler `fsm.on(\"transition\") {|from, to, evt| System.print(\"    [sfx]  transition %(from) -\u003e %(to) via %(evt)\") }` printed `null` per transition under `hatch run`. Workaround at the time was `+` concat; reverted to natural `%()` after the fix.\n\n**How to apply:** if a future \"closure prints null where it should print a string\" bug appears, first check whether the function is taking the threaded baseline path and look for a recently-added Instruction variant that falls into the `_ =\u003e op_noop` arm of `build_threaded`. Same shape of bug.\n\nRelated: [[feedback-verify-aot-against-tiered]] — same class of interpreter-vs-jit divergence.","files":null}]}